{"url": "https://www.famu.edu/students/international-education-and-development/index.php", "final_url": "https://www.famu.edu/students/international-education-and-development/index.php", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-11-13", "text": "International Education and Development\nApply\nVisit\nGive\nSkip to content\nburger opener\nMenu\nSearch\nnav close\nsearchsubmit\nopenerAcademics\nAcademic Affairs\nColleges and Schools\nCommencement\nContinuing Education and Professional Development\nCourse Catalog\nFAMU Online!\nGraduate Studies and Research\nLibraries\nRegistrar's Office\nStudy Abroad\nTest Service Bureau\nopenerAdmissions + Aid\nApply Now\nAdmissions\nFinancial Aid\nIgnite Transfer Program\nSchedule a Tour\nScholarships\nopenerStudent Life\nCommencement\nDining Services\nFinancial Aid\nHealth Services\nHonors Program\nHousing\nMarching 100\nRegistrar's Office\nStudent Accounts\nStudent Activities\nopenerAdministration\nBoard of Trustees\nOffice of the President\nChief Operating Officer\nAcademic Affairs\nAudit\nCommunications\nFaculty Senate\nFinance and Administration\nFoundation\nGovernment Relations\nInformation Technology\nLegal Affairs\nResearch\nSACS Accreditation\nStrategic Planning\nStudent Affairs\nTitle III\nUnited Faculty of Florida\nUniversity Advancement\nUniversity Policy Office\nopenerAbout FAMU\nHistory\nNews\nEvents\nStrategic Plan\nAT A GLANCEAT A GLANCE\nFAMMail\niRattler\nWorkDay\nCanvas\nGive\niStrike\nCareers @ FAMU\nDirectory\nFaculty\nAlumni\nAthletics\nNews\nEvents\nEmergency Alerts\nTitle IX\nUniversity Policies\nclosesearchsubmit\nInternational Education and Development\nThe Office of International Education and Development (OIED) has welcomed over 5,000\ninternational students and sent thousands of Florida Agricultural and Mechanical University\nstudents abroad since its establishment in 2003.\nOffice Of International Education & Development\nHome\nStudents\nScholarships\nCommencement\nNew Student Orientation\nInternational Education & Development\nRattler Pack\nDigital Rattler Initiative\nrattlerverse\nOffice Of International Education & Development\nAbout OIED & Staff\nDiplomat In Residence\nEducation Abroad\nForeign Travel\nDepartment Forms\nNational Student Exchange\nPassport Services\nRecruitment & Admissions\nInternational Student & Scholar Services\nThe mission of The Office of International Education and Development (OIED) is to foster campus internationalization and raise awareness of the value of international\neducation. We serve students, faculty, staff, and the community with the goal of creating\nleaders who possess the skills necessary to function in a globally interconnected\nworld.\nRely on the FAMU Community\nNo matter where you are from, we want your time at FAMU to be enriching and enjoyable.\nFor international students new to campus, the OIED is ready to answer all your questions\n\u2014 so you can focus on making new friends and immersing yourself in a new culture\nAbout OIED & Staff\nOIED was established in June 2003. Throughout the office\u2019s tenure on campus, it has\nwelcomed over 5,000 international students and scholars, and sent thousands of students\nabroad. Get To Know Us!\nEducation Abroad\nTake classes in a foreign country for a semester or even just a summer and expand\nyour horizons personally, academically, and professionally. New Horizons Ahead!\nForeign Travel\nRequest for Foreign Travel should be submitted to OIED a minimum of 35-40 days in\nadvance to ensure all parties have adequate time to sign the documentation and return\nit. Bon Voyage!\nForms\nDepartment Forms For OIED Fill Out Forms!\nInternational Student & Scholar Services\nWelcome to ISSS - where international students and scholars from more than 45 countries\nbelong to the FAMUly now! Welcome to ISSS!\nNational Student Exchange\nMore than 118,000 students have taken advantage of collegiate study away through NSE\nand new adventures begin daily. A New Adventure!\nPassport Services\nOIED at FAMU is a passport acceptance facility. We accept passports for FAMU students,\nemployees, as well as members of the community. Learn More!\nRecruitment & Admissions\nRegardless of your native land, once you enroll or join our research faculty, you\nbecome a valued member of the FAMU Community. Become A Rattler Today!\nSchool of Record\nFAMU is the School of Record for a number of Partner International Educational Organizations\naround the world. Learn More!\nContact Us\nLooking for a specific contact? Visit our \"About OIED & Staff\" page!\n302 Perry Paige North\n1740 S. Martin Luther King Blvd\nTallahassee, FL 32307\nP:\n850-599-3295\nF:\n850-561-2520 (fax)\nE:\noiedadmin@famu.edu\nApply\nVisit\nGive\nfab button\nBack to Top\n1601 S. Martin Luther King Jr Blvd, Tallahassee, FL 32307\nContact Us\n(850) 599-3000\nfacebook\ninstagram\ntwitter\nyoutube\nTerms of Use\nLegal Notice\nTitle IX\nEthics Hotline\nAccessibility\nFeedback\n\u00a9 2026 Florida Agricultural and Mechanical University.\nAll Rights Reserved\n\u00a9", "links": [["Apply", "https://admissions.famu.edu/index.php"], ["Visit", "https://www.famu.edu/students/new-student-orientation/campus-visits.php"], ["Give", "https://engage.famu.edu/g/donate"], ["Skip to content", "https://www.famu.edu/students/international-education-and-development/index.php#main"], ["", "https://www.famu.edu/index.php"], ["Academics", "https://www.famu.edu/academics/index.php"], ["Academic Affairs", "https://www.famu.edu/administration/academic-affairs/index.php"], ["Colleges and Schools", "https://www.famu.edu/academics/colleges-and-schools/index.php"], ["Commencement", "https://www.famu.edu/students/commencement/index.php"], ["Continuing Education and Professional Development", "https://www.famu.edu/academics/continuing-education-and-professional-development/index.php"], ["Course Catalog", "https://catalog.famu.edu"], ["FAMU Online!", "https://www.famu.edu/academics/famu-online/index.php"], ["Graduate Studies and Res